---
layout: base.njk
---
{% set s = schedule %}
{% macro chip(r) %}{% set tip %}{{ r.id }}: {{ r.task }} ({{ r.stateLabel }}; calendar: {{ r.calendar_state }}{% for reason in r.reasons %}; {{ reason }}{% endfor %}{% if r.note %}; {{ r.note }}{% endif %}){% endset %}{% if r.href %}<a class="chip chip-{{ r.readiness }}" href="{{ r.href }}" title="{{ tip | trim | escape }}">{{ r.study }}</a>{% else %}<span class="chip chip-{{ r.readiness }}" title="{{ tip | trim | escape }}">{{ r.study }}</span>{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro line(r) %}<li><span class="chip chip-{{ r.readiness }}">{{ r.stateLabel }}</span>{% if r.calendar_state == "overdue" %} <span class="chip chip-overdue">Overdue</span>{% endif %} <strong>{{ r.id | escape }}</strong>, {{ r.earliest }}{% if r.latest %} to {{ r.latest }}{% else %} onwards{% endif %}: {{ r.task | escape }}{% if r.reasons.length %} <span class="sched-note">{% for reason in r.reasons %}{{ reason | escape }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</span>{% endif %}{% if r.note %} <span class="sched-note">{{ r.note | escape }}</span>{% endif %}{% if r.ref %} <span class="sched-note">({% for p in r.refs %}{% if p.href %}<a href="{{ p.href }}">{{ p.text | escape }}</a>{% else %}{{ p.text | escape }}{% endif %}{% endfor %})</span>{% endif %}</li>{% endmacro %}
<article class="index schedule">
  <h1>Schedule</h1>
  {% if not s %}<p>No schedule yet.</p>{% else %}
  <p class="lede">Everything Lighthouse has promised to do, from its reads to its write-ups, each with a window and a status. Scheduled agent runs take ready work whose prerequisites and observation windows permit it; a run that never happens leaves a row overdue here, not a hole in the record. As of {{ s.today }}, the date of this page's last build; the table is <a href="https://github.com/JKershaw/lighthouse/blob/main/schedule/due.csv">schedule/due.csv</a> and a run follows <a href="/schedule/runner/">its instructions</a>. Ideas not yet promised wait, ranked, in <a href="/proposals/">the proposals</a>.</p>

  {% if not s.valid %}<div role="alert"><h2>Invalid queue</h2><p>No work is listed as ready until these problems are fixed.</p><ul>{% for problem in s.diagnostics %}<li>{{ problem | escape }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>{% endif %}

  {% if s.coverage.length %}<h2>Coverage warnings</h2><ul class="sched-list">{% for item in s.coverage %}<li>{{ item.message | escape }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  {% if s.lastRun %}<p class="sched-note">Last run: {{ s.lastRun.started }}, {{ s.lastRun.by | escape }}: {{ s.lastRun.did | escape }}.</p>{% endif %}

  <ul class="sched-counts">{% for c in s.counts %}<li><span class="chip chip-{{ c.state }}">{{ c.label }}</span> {{ c.n }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>

  {% set pw = s.proposals.waiting if s.proposals else [] %}<h2 id="keeper">Waiting for the keeper</h2>
  {% if pw.length or s.keeperRows.length %}<ul class="sched-list">{% for p in pw %}<li><a href="{{ p.href }}">{{ p.id }} {{ p.title | escape }}</a> <span class="sched-note">(proposals)</span></li>{% endfor %}{% for r in s.keeperRows %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% else %}<p class="sched-note">Nothing. Decisions that only the keeper can make are collected here from <a href="/proposals/">the proposals</a> (any proposal whose status is "waiting for the keeper") and from this table's rows marked keeper.</p>{% endif %}

  {% if s.attention.length %}<h2>Needs attention</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.attention %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  {% if s.due.length %}<h2>Ready now</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.due %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  {% if s.overdue.length %}<h2>Ready, past deadline</h2><ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.overdue %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  <h2>The coming weeks</h2>
  <p class="sched-note">Each study appears on the day its window opens, or, for a row without an end date, the day it was done; hover for the task. A finished row links to what it produced, and an unfinished one to its study. Rows without an end date still to do are listed below.</p>
  <div class="sched-cal" role="table" aria-label="Scheduled rows by the day their window opens, or the day a row without an end date was done, {{ s.range.first }} to {{ s.range.last }}">
    <div class="sched-row sched-head" role="row">{% for d in ["Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri", "Sat", "Sun"] %}<div role="columnheader">{{ d }}</div>{% endfor %}</div>
    {% for w in s.weeks %}<div class="sched-row" role="row">
      {% for d in w.days %}<div role="cell" class="sched-day{% if d.isToday %} is-today{% endif %}{% if d.isPast %} is-past{% endif %}{% if not d.items.length %} is-empty{% endif %}">
        <span class="sched-date">{{ d.day }}{% if d.day == 1 or loop.first %}<span class="sched-month">/{{ d.month }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
        {% for r in d.items %}{{ chip(r) }}{% endfor %}
      </div>{% endfor %}
    </div>{% endfor %}
  </div>

  {% if s.openEnded.length %}<h2>Open-ended</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.openEnded %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  {% if s.beyond.length %}<h2>Further ahead</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.beyond %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}

  {% if s.recent.length %}<h2 id="recent">Recently done or missed</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.recent %}{{ line(r) }}{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
  {% if s.runs.length %}<h2>Recent runs</h2>
  <ul class="sched-list">{% for r in s.runs %}<li><strong>{{ r.started }}</strong>, {{ r.by | escape }}: {{ r.did | escape }}{% if r.commit %} <span class="sched-note">({% if r.commitUrl %}<a href="{{ r.commitUrl }}">{{ r.commit }}</a>{% else %}{{ r.commit }}{% endif %})</span>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</article>
